// Whether export i survives emission, mirroring dce.id's own test for a
// function: kept when its owner is reachable, wherever pruning applies here.
// Pruning applies in two independent places:
//
//   * the test harness (back/tgt/c/emit/prog/test/unit/flag.id), which always
//     narrows `prog` and `rfn` to what a case reaches, so `is_harn` alone
//     decides -- the freestanding/no-main question below is about the
//     program, not the harness built beside it;
//   * the program itself, exactly where dce_prune decides to run at all: a
//     build with `main`, not `--freestanding` (nat_all_live, back/drive/sink/
//     natives/more/live.id, already answers "is anything pruned here").
//
// Outside both, nothing is pruned and every export survives, same as every
// function.
keep_export(int i) {
  int ok = 1;
  if(is_harn() == 1 || nat_all_live() == 0) {
    ok = is_reach((import eowners)[i]);
  }
} return int ok;
